            on itself. The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+quotient"} homotopy quotient
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Cyc
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ≔
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi ℒ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ⫽
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cyc(X) \;\coloneqq\; \mathcal{L}(X) \sslash S^1
            of this action might be called the
            %em cyclic loop space
            of
            = succeed ":" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
          %p
            If
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simply+connected+topological+space"} simply connected topological space
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ordinary+cohomology"} ordinary cohomology
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Cyc
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cyc(X)
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cyclic+cohomology"} cyclic cohomology
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            (Jones’ theorem &amp;lbrack;
            %a{:href => "#Jones87"}> Jones (1987)
            ;
            = succeed ";" do
              %a{:href => "#Loday92"} Loday (1992), §7.2
            = succeed "&rbrack;," do
              %a{:href => "#Loday15"} Loday (2015)
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#RelationToCyclicCohomology"} below
          %p
            Analogously, if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo =
                  %mi Spec
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X = Spec(A)
            is an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/affine+variety"} affine variety
            regarded in
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+algebraic+geometry"} derived algebraic geometry
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒪
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ℒ
                  %mi Spec
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{O}(\mathcal{L}Spec(A))
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hochschild+homology"} Hochschild homology
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒪
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ℒ
                  %mi Spec
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{O}((\mathcal{L}Spec(A))/S^1)
            the corresponding
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cyclic+homology"} cyclic homology
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hochschild+cohomology"} Hochschild cohomology
          %p
            But
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Cyc
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cyc(X)
            is also known as the
            %em string space
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            (
            %a{:href => "#Chataur05"}> Chataur 2005. 4.8.1
            ,
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#BokstedtOttosen05"} Bökstedt &amp; Ottosen 05, p. 1
          %p#StapletonTerminology
            If
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo =
                  %mi Y
                  %mo ⫽
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X = Y\sslash G
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+quotient"} homotopy quotient
            of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
            by a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+group"} topological group
            action, regarded as a locally constant
            = succeed "-stack," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
            = succeed "-model" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/point-set+topology"} point set
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+loop+space"} free loop space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℒ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Y
                  %mo ⫽
                  %mi G
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{L}(Y \sslash G)
            has been called the
            %em twisted loop space
            in
            = succeed ";" do
              %a{:href => "#Witten88"} Witten 88
            %a{:href => "#Stapleton13"} Stapleton (2013), p. 2
            in the context of the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/transchromatic+character"} transchromatic character
          %p
            A candidate lift of this construction from plain
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+types"} homotopy types
            to
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+homotopy+types"} smooth homotopy types
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orbifold"} orbifold
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stacks"} stacks
            = succeed "-construction." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Huan%27s+inertia+orbifold"} Huan's inertia orbifold
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#AsRightBaseChange
            As right base change along
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo *
                  %mo →
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \ast \to \mathbf{B} S^1
          %p
            The cyclic loop space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℒ
                  %mi X
                  %mo ⫽
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{L}X  \sslash S^1
            is equivalently the right
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/base+change"} base change
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dependent+product"} dependent product
            along the canonical point inclusion
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo *
                  %mo →
                  %mi B
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \ast \to B S^1
            (
            %a{:href => "base+change#CyclicLoopSpace"}> this prop.
            ) into the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/delooping"} delooping
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^1
            (the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classifying+space"} classifying space
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/circle+group"} circle group
            when realized in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classical+model+structure+on+topological+spaces"} homotopy theory of
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+spaces"} topological spaces
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/double+dimensional+reduction"} double dimensional reduction
            (
            %a{:href => "#BMSS19"}> BMSS 19, Sec. 2.2
            , following
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#FSS18"} FSS 18, Sec. 3
          %h3#RelationToCyclicCohomology
            Ordinary cohomology of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℒ
                  %mi X
                  %mo ⫽
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{L}X \sslash S^1
            as cyclic cohomology of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            be a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simply+connected+topological+space"} simply connected
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ordinary+cohomology"} ordinary cohomology
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi H
                    %mo •
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H^\bullet
            of its
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+loop+space"} free loop space
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hochschild+homology"} Hochschild homology
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi HH
                    %mo •
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} HH_\bullet
            of its
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/singular+cohomology"} singular chains
            = succeed ":" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^\bullet(X)
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi H
                    %mo •
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ℒ
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≃
                  %msub
                    %mi HH
                    %mo •
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi C
                    %mo •
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  H^\bullet(\mathcal{L}X)
                  \\simeq
                  HH_\bullet( C^\bullet(X) )
                  \\,.
          %p
            Moreover the
            = succeed "-equivariant" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^1
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℒ
                  %mi X
                  %mo ⫽
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{L}X \sslash S^1
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cyclic+homology"} cyclic homology
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi HC
                    %mo •
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} HC_\bullet
            of the singular chains:
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi H
                    %mo •
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ℒ
                  %mi X
                  %mo ⫽
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≃
                  %msub
                    %mi HC
                    %mo •
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi C
                    %mo •
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  H^\bullet(\mathcal{L}X \sslash S^1)
                  \\simeq
                  HC_\bullet( C^\bullet(X) )
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#Jones87"}> Jones 87, Thm. A
            , review in
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Loday92"} Loday 92, Cor. 7.3.14
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#Loday11"} Loday 11, Sec. 4
          %p
            If the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coefficients"} coefficients
            are
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rational+numbers"} rational
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+type"} finite type
            then this may be computed by the
            = succeed "," do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Sullivan+model+for+free+loop+spaces"} Sullivan model for free loop spaces
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a{:href => "Sullivan+model+of+free+loop+space#RelationToHochschildHomology"} Relation to Hochschild homology
          %p
            In the special case that the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            carries the structure of a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifold"} smooth manifold
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            are equivalent to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dgc-algebra"} dgc-algebra
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+forms"} differential forms
            (the
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/de+Rham+algebra"} de Rham algebra
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi H
                    %mo •
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ℒ
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≃
                  %msub
                    %mi HH
                    %mo •
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi Ω
                    %mo •
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  H^\bullet(\mathcal{L}X)
                  \\simeq
                  HH_\bullet( \Omega^\bullet(X) )
                  \\,.
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi H
                    %mo •
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ℒ
                  %mi X
                  %mo ⫽
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≃
                  %msub
                    %mi HC
                    %mo •
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi Ω
                    %mo •
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  H^\bullet(\mathcal{L}X \sslash S^1)
                  \\simeq
                  HC_\bullet( \Omega^\bullet(X) )
                  \\,.
          %p
            This is known as
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jones%27+theorem"} Jones' theorem
            (
            %a{:href => "#Jones87"}> Jones 87
            )
          %p
            An
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28infinity%2C1%29-category+theory"} infinity-category theoretic
            proof of this fact is indicated at
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a{:href => "Hochschild+cohomology#JonesTheorem"} Hochschild cohomology – Jones’ theorem
          %h3#StableSplitting Stable splitting
          %p
          .num_prop
            %h6 Proposition
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ∈
                    %msup
                      %mi TopSpaces
                      %mrow
                        %mo *
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \in TopSpaces^{\ast/}
              a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pointed+topological+space"} pointed topological space
              with
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reduced+suspension"} reduced suspension
              denoted
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Σ
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma X
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stabilization"} stabilization
              of its cyclic loop spaces splits as a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/direct+sum"} direct sum
              of
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/suspension+spectra"} suspension spectra
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinite+loop+space"} infinite loop space
              of that as a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/product+space"} product space
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi Ω
                      %mn ∞
                    %msup
                      %mi Σ
                      %mn ∞
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                    %mi Maps
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Σ
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⫽
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ≃
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi Ω
                      %mn ∞
                    %msup
                      %mi Σ
                      %mn ∞
                    %mi B
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                    %mo ×
                    %munder
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                      %mrow
                        %mi k
                        %mo ∈
                        %msub
                          %mi ℕ
                          %mo +
                    %msup
                      %mi Ω
                      %mn ∞
                    %msup
                      %mi Σ
                      %mn ∞
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi E
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi k
